NAME
       sshd - secure shell server

SYNOPSIS
       sshd [-p port] [-f hostkey] [-c]

DESCRIPTION
       Accepts SSH-2 connections and gives each one a shell on a
       pseudo-terminal. Password and public key authentication are both
       supported; keys are read from the account's authorized_keys.

OPTIONS
       -p N   listen on port N instead of 22
       -f F   use F as the host key
       -c     stay in the foreground

FILES
       ~/.ssh/authorized_keys

SEE ALSO
       ssh(1), ssh-keygen(1), passwd(1)
